{"version":"1","id":"thevimeagen","handle":"thevimeagen","name":"TheVimeagen","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--afAlRBlr--/f_auto/v1712314182/logos/thevimeagen","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-6.5411,"y":-9.5889,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":84,"newest_post_at":"2025-12-09T21:28:11.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2023-09-29T18:27:48.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.029762,"listicle_ratio":0.02381,"question_ratio":0.011905,"avg_read_time":64.428571,"summary_length_avg":273.510204,"title_length_avg":33.47619,"title_length_var":168.606576,"tag_entropy":2.73734,"tag_diversity":0.52381,"top_tag_share":0.02381,"avg_upvotes":5.47619,"median_upvotes":1.0,"avg_comments":0.107143,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.021692,"zero_engagement_share":0.404762,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.958517,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.02439},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[4.9118,-3.0882],"cadence_depth":[-1.3235,9.8088],"hype_variety":[6.6618,-4.4853],"title_style":[-1.2941,5.8676]},"top_tags":[["vim",41],["golang",41],["rust",38],["javascript",38],["webdev",37],["bash",35],["typescript",32],["game-development",10]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["John Carmack's unique approach to coding excellence","The Greatest Vim Website","I Tried Golf.Vim"],"outlier":["Building a precise AI coding assistant that generates functions without restructuring code"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"ijx5ubsIb","title":"Building a precise AI coding assistant that generates functions without restructuring code","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MNvciiZ5x9A","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-think-this-is-what-ai-should-look-like-ijx5ubsib","summary":"A developer shares their custom AI coding assistant called Project 99, designed to generate code within narrow, precise scopes rather than large refactors. The tool uses tree-sitter to identify the function containing the cursor and fills in implementation details while preserving the developer's API design and code structure. This approach aims to combine autocomplete-style precision with AI generation speed, keeping developers engaged and in control of architecture decisions.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/MNvciiZ5x9A/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-09T21:28:11.000Z"},{"id":"43KS6t9WT","title":"I Am a Making Game on ESP Micro V2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5JXS4fc7iTU","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-am-a-making-game-on-esp-micro-v2-43ks6t9wt","summary":"A developer shares their journey building a handheld game console on ESP Play Micro V2 hardware, achieving 700+ FPS through custom memory management techniques. The project uses direct memory access (DMA), splits the 320x240 screen into 8-row regions to work around RAM constraints, and implements dirty region tracking to minimize screen updates. The developer discusses their approach to handling internal RAM vs PS RAM limitations, asynchronous rendering, and creating a web-based asset upload system using Phoenix/Elixir for their son to contribute game art.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/5JXS4fc7iTU/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-13T17:27:42.000Z"},{"id":"DEzuO8h34","title":"WAYBAR","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fGhkRiUsTpc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/waybar-dezuo8h34","summary":"The post dives into configuring Waybar, a status bar for Wayland, using JSON and CSS for styling. It discusses modules available for workspaces, system tray, battery, clock, and network. The post also covers community usage and integration with Hyperland.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/fGhkRiUsTpc/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-05-08T19:38:16.000Z"},{"id":"KY0AgvXhE","title":"I Tried Golf.Vim","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AoMfifC6QyI","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-tried-golf-vim-ky0agvxhe","summary":"The post explores the experience of integrating a game called Vim Golf with the Vim editor to enhance coding skills through keystroke challenges. The author attempts various strategies to optimize keystrokes and reflects on the fun yet challenging aspects of the game. The concept highlights the use of games for improving technical proficiency with Vim.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/AoMfifC6QyI/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":47,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-05-07T15:00:30.000Z"},{"id":"Y07bAkS0g","title":"HEAVY ARCH RICING Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J4xU2rOMh3I","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/heavy-arch-ricing-part-2-y07baks0g","summary":"The post describes a user struggling to improve their Arch Linux setup, specifically dealing with keyboard issues and launching applications without a terminal. The user discusses configuring XKB files to fix the keyboard functionality and explores different configurations to streamline their workflow. There is also mention of difficulties with Hyperland and managing keybindings.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/J4xU2rOMh3I/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-05-07T04:12:22.000Z"},{"id":"ov1XcxL3g","title":"Ricing Arch Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UzUu77RZGSE","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ricing-arch-part-1-ov1xcxl3g","summary":"The author describes their experience and challenge installing Arch Linux from a USB stick, emphasizing the frustrations and successes while booting and configuring the system. They face technical difficulties with slow startup, sound issues, and deciding between installation options. The post offers insights into the complexities of Arch Linux installation and customization, including Hyperland setup and issues with system configuration.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UzUu77RZGSE/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-05-05T23:18:54.000Z"},{"id":"vDDPBV7Yg","title":"Building A Copilot Like AutoComplete!!","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GuRiTCX-rT0","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/building-a-copilot-like-autocomplete--vddpbv7yg","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/GuRiTCX-rT0/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":9,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-08T17:06:37.000Z"},{"id":"wNgp56Fvh","title":"Nuking A Twitter Community","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZWLljD4iwpM","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/nuking-a-twitter-community-wngp56fvh","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ZWLljD4iwpM/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":8,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-21T20:00:02.000Z"},{"id":"Vawlwb1gO","title":"John Carmack's unique approach to coding excellence","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yfIgOMb2jmU","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-can-he-be-so-good--vawlwb1go","summary":"John Carmack, praised for his groundbreaking approach to coding, wrote every function from scratch for game engines like Doom. This approach reflected his deep understanding and control over the coding process, contrasting the modern trend of using libraries. While Carmack's methods may seem extreme, they underline the importance of skill, control, and efficiency in software development. Additionally, improving typing speed can significantly enhance a programmer's productivity and mental focus.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/yfIgOMb2jmU/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":52,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2025-01-18T16:00:57.000Z"},{"id":"yY9Gr5ZXq","title":"Navigating a technical interview with AI","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9MXlwBi5gLk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-got-interviewed-by-an-ai-yy9gr5zxq","summary":"A software engineer nervously prepares for a technical interview with an AI, discussing challenges in creating and optimizing command-line tools, scripting in various programming languages, and tackling communication during interviews. The discussion also involves the struggles of handling unexpected questions and the role of effective communication in interviews.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/9MXlwBi5gLk/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":9,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-17T14:05:51.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["lauriewired","aidotengineer","TechWithTim","mentaloutlaw","tsoding_daily"],"opposite_handles":["horde","watercooler","dailydevworld","on_leuwcq","devtools"],"similar":[{"id":"lauriewired","handle":"lauriewired","name":"LaurieWired","is_squad":false,"x":-6.5224,"y":-9.4755,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":89,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--PWgKO8OW--/f_auto/v1713076011/logos/lauriewired","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.861135,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.039326,"avg_read_time":13.426966,"tag_diversity":0.719101},"top_tags_preview":[["malware",17],["reverse-engineering",17],["security",13]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[7.3529,6.3971],"cadence_depth":[-1.0,7.6765],"hype_variety":[7.6029,5.0147],"title_style":[7.2353,3.3529]}},{"id":"aidotengineer","handle":"aidotengineer","name":"AI Engineer","is_squad":false,"x":-6.5937,"y":-9.7625,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":377,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--u5PucxNT--/f_auto/v1724338940/logos/aidotengineer","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":4.764307,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.005305,"avg_read_time":26.888594,"tag_diversity":0.519894},"top_tags_preview":[["ai-agents",133],["ai",118],["llm",112]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-3.2941,-2.2353],"cadence_depth":[7.6029,9.1765],"hype_variety":[-1.2059,8.1471],"title_style":[-9.7941,0.0294]}},{"id":"TechWithTim","handle":"TechWithTim","name":"Tech With Tim","is_squad":false,"x":-6.7326,"y":-9.593,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":378,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--6vVIDfU0--/f_auto/v1711726146/logos/TechWithTim","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":3.654274,"median_upvot